  "label": "historical event",
  "description": "The phrase 'historical spacecraft explosion' implies a reference to past spaceflight disasters, which requires background knowledge to understand the meme. Background knowledge includes understanding that there have been real historical spacecraft explosions, such as the Challenger disaster (1986) or the Columbia disaster (2003), which are well-documented events in spaceflight history. The meme uses this knowledge to create a false juxtaposition, implying that the image depicts a historical disaster, when in fact it shows a successful launch. This requires the audience to be aware of the history of spaceflight and its associated risks.",
